    {
      "id": "s2017-e2-q09",
      "number": 9,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "The area of the region of the plane bounded by the curves $y = 4x - x^2$ and $y = x^2$ is equal to $\\frac{8}{3}$. The $y$-coordinate of its centroid is equal to",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$3$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{3}{2}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac{4}{3}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$2$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "E",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L9"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 6,
      "solution": "The curves meet where $4x - x^2 = x^2$, so $4x = 2x^2$: $x = 0$ and $x = 2$. On $[0, 2]$ the parabola $y = 4x - x^2$ is on top and $y = x^2$ is below. With $A = \\frac{8}{3}$,\n\n$$\n\\bar{y} = \\frac{1}{A}\\int_0^2 \\frac{1}{2}\\left[(4x - x^2)^2 - x^4\\right]dx = \\frac{3}{16}\\int_0^2 (4x - 2x^2)\\,4x\\,dx = \\frac{3}{2}\\int_0^2 (2x^2 - x^3)\\,dx\n$$\n\n$$\n= \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}x^3 - \\frac{x^4}{4}\\right)\\Big|_0^2 = \\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\frac{16}{3} - \\frac{16}{4}\\right) = 24\\left(\\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{4}\\right) = 2.\n$$",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2017-e2-q10",
      "number": 10,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "Compute $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\left(\\frac{n^2+2n-4}{2n-5} - \\frac{n}{2}\\right)$",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac{3}{4}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{9}{4}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac{7}{4}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$0$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$\\infty$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L20"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 6,
      "solution": "$$\n\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\left(\\frac{n^2+2n-4}{2n-5} - \\frac{n}{2}\\right) = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{2n^2 + 4n - 8 - 2n^2 + 5n}{2(2n-5)} = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{9n - 8}{4n - 10} = \\frac{9}{4}.\n$$",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2017-e2-q11",
      "number": 11,
      "points": 8,
      "stem": "The sum of the series $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1+2^n}{5^n}$ is equal to",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac{6}{5}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{9}{5}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$\\frac{11}{12}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{12}{5}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "E",
          "text": "$\\frac{8}{9}$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "C",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L21"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 7,
      "solution": "$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1+2^n}{5^n} = \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^n + \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac{2}{5}\\right)^n = \\frac{1/5}{1 - 1/5} + \\frac{2/5}{1 - 2/5} = \\frac{1/5}{4/5} + \\frac{2/5}{3/5} = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{3 + 8}{12} = \\frac{11}{12}.\n$$",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2017-e2-q12",
      "number": 12,
      "points": 4,
      "stem": "The series $\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{4n+5}{n^2}$ converges by the integral test",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "True"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "False"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "B",
      "lessonIds": [
        "L22"
      ],
      "sourcePage": 7,
      "solution": "False: the series diverges. For large $n$, $\\frac{4n+5}{n^2}$ behaves like $\\frac{1}{n}$, and\n\n$$\n\\int_1^{\\infty} \\frac{4x+5}{x^2}\\,dx = \\int_1^{\\infty} \\frac{4}{x}\\,dx + \\int_1^{\\infty} \\frac{5}{x^2}\\,dx,\n$$\n\nwhere the first integral diverges.",
      "status": "reviewed"
    },
    {
